      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T12:47:50Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the proxy deployment and initialization receipts, exploit receipt and call trace, complete Upgraded-event history through the incident, EIP-1967 slot values around each final change, exploit-time implementation bytecode, and both attacker-artifact creation transactions. The proxy emitted four Upgraded events before the incident: its initial audited implementation, two events in the attacker initialization transaction, and the final pre-incident selection of 0x4c4eacbe5d5232698d12c379be14a0e561001c21 at block 23939725. Storage confirms 0x4c4e...1c21 remained selected through block 23941342. The exploit first delegates upgradeToAndCall to that artifact and switches to 0xa3d2616ee942b36648eaa55976ee7b761bd2a21b inside the drain transaction; later victim calls execute the latter. Both are attacker-installed drain machinery, so the prior 78-day audited-implementation age is not an exploit-executed-code measurement. Receipt transfers establish 236.842877402051689989 stETH and 302,908.856746 USDC lost."
    },
